### 5.1 Data Dictionary & Schema Constraints

* **`TRANSACTIONS.executed_rate`:** Stored as `DECIMAL(18, 8)` to eliminate precision loss on high-value pairings (e.g., JPY, KWD).
* **`DRAWER_INVENTORY.bill_count`:** Constrained with check condition `CHECK (bill_count >= 0)`. Negative inventories are structurally prevented at the database constraint layer.
* **`AML_ALERTS.status`:** State-machine constrained to: `PENDING_SUPERVISOR_OVERRIDE`, `APPROVED`, `BLOCKED_SAR_FILED`.

