## Module 6: AML/KYC Regulatory Framework & State Machine

Every physical cash trade moves through a deterministic compliance state machine:

```
                      [Initiate Transaction]
                                │
                                ▼
                   {Amount >= $10,000 Equiv?}
                                │
               ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
               │ YES                             │ NO
               ▼                                 ▼
    [Mandatory KYC Triggered]            {Customer in Watchlist?}
    - National ID / Passport                       │
    - Purpose of Exchange                          ├──────────────┐
    - Occupation & Source                          ▼ YES          ▼ NO
               │                        [BLOCK & FILE SAR]  [Standard Execution]
               ▼                                                  │
    [Chief Teller Review]                                         ▼
    - Verify Physical ID                                    [Generate Receipt]
    - Sanctions List Screening                                    │
               │                                                  ▼
     ┌─────────┴─────────┐                                [Update Vault Ledger]
     │ Approve           │ Reject
     ▼                   ▼
[Supervisor Auth]   [Halt Trade &
- Sign-off Token     Log Flag]

```

### 6.1 Regulatory Thresholds

1. **Simplified Due Diligence (SDD):** $<\$1,000$. Standard receipt issued; minimal identification required.
2. **Customer Due Diligence (CDD):** $\$1,000 \le \text{Amount} < \$10,000$. Government identification logged into system; name checked against local PEP (Politically Exposed Persons) databases.
3. **Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD):** $\ge \$10,000$. Mandatory Currency Transaction Report (CTR) file generated. Proof of funds documentation captured and dual-key chief teller sign-off required.

