## Module 8: System Implementation Details (Frontend & State Engine)

### 8.1 Single-File Architecture Rationale

The standalone application combines presentation (HTML5/Tailwind), state management (reactive JavaScript modules), visual graphing (HTML5 Canvas vector charts), and sound synthesis (Web Audio API) without external bundle dependencies.

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                    APPLICATION RUNTIME                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  1. State Store (`appState`)                                                          |
|     - Active Station Pointer (`retail`, `vip`, `corporate`, `express`)                |
|     - FX Pair Dictionary (EUR/USD, GBP/USD, USD/JPY, etc.) with Mid/Spread/Trend      |
|     - Drawer Inventory Matrix (Currency x Denomination counts)                        |
|     - Transaction Ledger History & Token Queue Queue Stack                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  2. Calculation Service Layer                                                         |
|     - `calculateExchange()`: Parses amounts, fees, and spread margins                 |
|     - `updateDenominationCount()`: Enforces drawer balance constraints                |
|     - `evaluateAML()`: Evaluates risk metrics based on customer data & trade size      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  3. Presentation & Audio Engine                                                        |
|     - Dynamic DOM renderer with localized number formatters                           |
|     - Canvas 2D engine rendering real-time historical micro-charts                    |
|     - Web Audio API Sound Synthesizer (audible frequency chime alerts)                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

```

### 8.2 Security Considerations for Counter Terminals

* **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Sanitization:** All customer-supplied inputs (names, passport numbers, trade purposes) are escaped through DOM text-node injection rather than unescaped `innerHTML`.
* **Session Locking:** Inactivity timers lock counter interfaces after 120 seconds of idle time, requiring cashier biometric or PIN re-entry to prevent unauthorized trades while away from the desk.

